# Google Drive OAuth (Development Overrides)
# Synca is an installed (public) OAuth client: the client ID shipped in
# release builds is committed in daemon/internal/auth/oauth.go and is not
# confidential. These variables only override the committed value during
# local development.
#
# Get a client ID from Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com
# Create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app".
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Google's token endpoint requires the client secret even for desktop-app
# clients. Release builds embed it at compile time from the protected
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET Actions secret (see Makefile: DAEMON_LDFLAGS), so
# users of released binaries never configure it. Local builds may set it here
# or in the environment instead; the runtime value takes precedence over the
# embedded one. NEVER commit this file — it is gitignored.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
